{
  "name": "Webhook Dedupe · 1 Receiver (Postgres)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Webhook Dedupe · Receiver on Postgres\n`POST dedupe/postgres` with a JSON body that has an `id`. The event is handled once, however many times and however close together it is delivered.\n\n**Claim** is one statement on a table with `event_key` as primary key. Exactly one run gets its own token back. A claim that failed, or that has been `processing` longer than the lease, can be taken by the next delivery in the same statement.\n\n**Mark done** and **Mark failed** only change the row while it still carries this run's token.\n\nSettings are at the top of the **Event** node. Put your own call in **Do the work**; it gets the event key as `Idempotency-Key`.",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 340,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "1745431f-725b-42df-839e-769283e37deb",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### The conflict path\n- **Duplicate: done** answers `200`. The event was handled, the sender can stop.\n- **Duplicate: in progress** answers `409`. Another run holds the claim and has not finished. A `2xx` here would tell the sender to stop while that run can still crash. With `409` it retries later and then finds the event done, failed or stale.\n- **Failed** answers `500` and frees the claim, so the next delivery runs again.\n- **Superseded**: this run was so slow that a retry took the claim over. It may not mark the event done.\n\nIf your sender gives up after a few non-2xx answers, change `409` to `200` and accept that a crash in that moment needs a manual replay.",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 300,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "1681ade7-6dbf-47d8-8dcb-3efe0e0ca1d6",
      "name": "Conflict",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1540,
        -400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "dedupe/postgres",
        "authentication": "headerAuth",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "e06d771e-0814-4a9f-87b1-5c2e905c64be",
      "name": "Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        0,
